    "question": {
      ":question/id": "cb22c996-863f-5590-b143-c680605dc7b7",
      ":question/problem": "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1}{x+9}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, let $u=x+9.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe can now rewrite the integral in terms of $u,$ solve it, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{x+9}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+9|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
